{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/595414-healing-the-world-through-the-dreaming","id":595414,"title":"Healing the world through the Dreaming?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-18T23:42:12-07:00","id":595414,"title":"Healing the world through the Dreaming?","content":"You are explicitly capable of fixing the world through the Umbra. If you perma kill a spirit of toxic waste, you force it to decompose. If you kill the spirit of a disease that is killing a man, you can save his life. If you go on an umbral vision quest, you can change the fate of a city. But what about the Dreaming? I've been rereading Dreams and Nightmares, and so much seems wrong in the Dreaming because of mortals losing their way, but if the problems in the Dreaming were fixed there, would mortals in the Waking World benefit from these victories?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T02:23:47-07:00","id":595492,"title":"","content":"Well, as far as I can remember Changeling metaphysics, not quite. Whyle the Umbra is made in the notion of an other side of the same reallity, the Dreaming is just an &quot;aftereffect&quot; of human experience. Your better chance would be to use Glamour to make people experience the Dreaming for a moment.<br /> <br /> In that regard, Changeling is a lot more about bringing the change to this gritty, static world in the hard way. Change the world by changing the people who live in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-28T11:19:05-08:00","id":818596,"title":"","content":"However from a Mage perspective (yes, i know. Crossover stuff. Get over it.), reality is the representation of what humanity dreams and believes, even unconsciously... <br /> I think if you managed to change something significant in the Dreaming, the effects would be felt in the Autumn World as belief shifts.<br /> If, for example, you managed to destroy completely Capeccia (and assuming it does represent humanity's belief in technological advance), technology would be affected all over the world. Again, as I said, this is crossover stuff, and most STs would not allow it. Except of course for those who would and who would encourage their players to do something like this so that they'll have a post-apocalyptic setting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10198-luisarmander","name":"Luisarmander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T07:51:41-08:00","id":819243,"title":"","content":"Fixing the world of Changeling: The Dreaming isn't as simple (heh, &quot;simple&quot;) as changing the collective heart of humanity on Earth or conquering the Dreaming's nightmares. The fae brought about the Shattering themselves. They forgot things that should never have been forgotten, neglected things that never should have been neglected, and broke things that should never have been broken.<br /> <br /> There was a time when the Kithain might have been powerful enough to realize their mistakes and take steps to fix it, but they didn't. They ran away and hid from their problems, some on Earth and some in Arcadia. In the intervening the centuries, the Kithain waned, becoming mere shadows of their former selves. The worlds were on a slow, but certain course toward their end caught between implacable banality on one side and overwhelming nightmare on the other. Miraculously, humanity gave the fae a second chance. The Resurgence gave pause to the rise of banality and nightmare, reunited the fae, and rekindled a small spark of their glamour. So far, the Kithain have done nothing but squander their opportunity, engaging in pointless wars and petty squabbles among themselves - the very same behavior that caused the Shattering in the first place.<br /> <br /> Something happened relatively recently that might be able to shake the Kithain up and get them to realize they're on the wrong track, but that's wholly the province of the PCs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T13:57:01-08:00","id":819489,"title":"","content":"I like PookaKnight's description of things. It would be interesting to play a Changeling game where it's touched on; give players a taste of what they WERE, when they COULD have done something, and now they have a second chance, just maybe, despite their lessened state, to push things back in the right direction. Find that which was neglected, which in their pride and arrogance they thought they could trash without consequence, and now repair it. Sort of the Once-Lers (but actually DOING something about it) of the supernatural world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-29T16:56:10-08:00","id":819585,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Segev</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/595414-healing-the-world-through-the-dreaming?p=819489#post819489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It would be interesting to play a Changeling game where it's touched on; give players a taste of what they WERE, when they COULD have done something, and now they have a second chance\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a game kinda like this that I've wanted to run, but will probably never get to; the overall Chronicle will be divided into three parts, each one with some heavy time dilation.<br /> <br /> During the first part, players make Raksha characters using Exalted rules. The first few sessions will play like an Exalted game. The last few sessions will move into the late Stone Age/early Bronze Age, but will keep using Exalted rules.<br /> <br /> The second part will take place in the late Bronze Age/Early Iron Age, using the same characters (more or less) but using DA:F rules. This part will play out like a like a standard DA:F game (albeit with typical Gonzo Nazfool Zest) until the Shattering. In my head canon, the Shattering goes a little different than it did in DA: DS.<br /> <br /> Finally, the third part will take place during CtD with the same basic character with significant mechanical alterations. Depending on the player, the characters may or not have some recollections of the mythic eras (i.e., Remembrance).<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know what it would mean for the characters, but I\u2019ve been curious to see how players respond to watching the power of their avatars diminish over several epochs.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":302,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","user":"Nazfool","date":". 01-29-2016, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T05:31:41-08:00","id":820903,"title":"","content":"I'd have fun in such a game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/827-segev","name":"Segev","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1001"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}